# What NOT to upload when deploying from the CLI (`vercel --prod`).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `.git/info/exclude` keeps the client photo drops and the
# annual report out of GIT, and that is all it does — Vercel's CLI does not read
# it. Without the entries below the CLI uploaded the entire working directory:
# 938MB, and a deploy that failed outright on "File size limit exceeded (100MB)"
# because one of the drops is a 490MB zip. Nothing in here is read by the build.
#
# A push-triggered deploy builds from the repository and was never affected —
# this only bites the CLI path, which is exactly the one reached for when a
# push-triggered deploy needs re-running.

# Working documents, Apps Script generators, brochures, client photo drops.
# Nothing under here is imported by the app; the published crops live in public/.
references/
references_2/

# Local build output and caches — Vercel builds its own.
.next/
.vercel/
.preview/

# Local env. Production values live in Vercel's own environment settings.
.env.local
.env*.local
